%% The life of one agent signal, and how the team's own decisions feed back into
%% how confident the next one is allowed to sound.
stateDiagram-v2
  direction TB
  [*] --> raised: a run finds evidence
  raised --> open: shown with evidence, source and confidence

  open --> accepted: facilitator accepts
  open --> dismissed: facilitator dismisses, with a reason
  open --> snoozed: not now
  snoozed --> open: the next run re-raises it
  accepted --> [*]
  dismissed --> [*]

  state proposal {
    [*] --> pending: written as one approvable line
    pending --> approved: a human approves
    pending --> rejected: a human rejects
    approved --> applied: the item changes and the event is logged
    applied --> undone: event.undone reverses it
  }

  open --> proposal: the signal proposes a tracker change

  note right of dismissed
    Dismissals are counted per signal kind.
    After 3 decisions, stated confidence becomes
    the average of the prior and the observed
    accept rate. Above 30 percent dismissal the
    detector is retuned rather than ignored.
  end note
